                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_12\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit narrows the RTL character range check in TextUtils.java from\n`(c >= 0xFE70 && c <= 0xFEFF)` to `(c >= 0xFE70 && c <= 0xFEFE)`, because\n0xFEFF is a special Unicode marker (BOM / zero-width no-break space) that\nshould not be treated as an RTL character.\n\nSearching all 13 candidates for the `isRTLCharacter` method (the only place\nthis range check exists) shows it is introduced for the first time in\ncandidate_12. That commit adds the entire method:\n\n    public static boolean isRTLCharacter(char c) {\n        //range of RTL characters per unicode specification\n        return (c >= 0x0590 && c <= 0x05FF) ||\n               (c >= 0xFB1D && c <= 0xFB4F) ||\n               (c >= 0x0600 && c <= 0x07BF) ||\n               (c >= 0xFB50 && c <= 0xFDFF) ||\n               (c >= 0xFE70 && c <= 0xFEFF)    ;\n    }\n\nThis is exactly the buggy range (inclusive of 0xFEFF) that the fix later\ncorrects. No earlier candidate (01 through 11) contains this method or range\ncheck at all, confirming candidate_12 is the first commit to introduce the\nproblematic code.\n\nNote: candidate_13 contains a diff that is byte-for-byte identical to the\nfix_commit_diff.txt (same blob hashes 88f725945..54bb57f0a and the exact\nFEFF->FEFE change), meaning candidate_13 is actually the fix commit itself\nrather than a bug-introducing candidate. It was therefore excluded from\nconsideration as the introducer.\n"
